Gaster.DisplayName: Mysterious Man

Dialogue: {
	Admin: {
		GoblinDialogue: I'm studying anomalies daily to get a proper grasp on what is happening, {0}'s ability to scam the same person multiple times might be related.
		GenericDialogue1: It's such a tragedy how easily something can go wrong, even if you don't expect it. Just look at this world, so many problems all at once.
		GenericDialogue2: Magic Mirrors tend to react weirdly to certain energies. I know that a patch of some very unique liquid energy appeared somewhere on this continent, I just don't remember where exactly. Maybe try dousing one of those mirrors in that liquid.
		GenericDialogue3: I've had a weird feeling since a while, it's as if everything could go mad any second...
		GenericDialogue4: Sometimes I ponder if he is still waiting for me... Oh apologies, I was absorbed in thought, do you need anything.
		GenericDialogue5: I would love to introduce you to the great team of multidimensional heroes that I work with, they are probably pretty busy right now though.
		GenericDialogue6: Ever had a problem where you became incredibly rich because of frogs and crackers? Well let me tell you about that one time where... What? What's that look supposed to mean, I'm telling the truth!
		GenericDialogue7: So how is this world? Having fun? Any suggestions for improvement? Haha I'm joking of course, I already spent 48 tries and several millenia to make this one. I also forgot my admin password.
		GenericDialogue8: I could have sworn that Angel Statue flipped me off one time. What do you mean 'what statue?', it's right over th- Alright I think living for this long has turned my brain to mush.
		GenericDialogue9: You cannot imagine how badly I want to eat some pizza right now, but this world is too primitive to have invented a pizza oven yet, and mine is out of reach. Maybe I could craft one in my forge?
		GenericDialogue10: Have you ever questioned what's beyond the stars? What vast world lies out there? Well, if you did, then stop. It's for the better to not know anything.
		GenericDialogue11: Thanks again for powering that beacon, I couldn't have come here to help without it. What its name is supposed to mean? Of course it means 'Caelis Number-48 Version-01 Data Transfer Beacon'. Though I do prefer to just call them Baby Tower.
		GenericDialogue12: I hope I can fix everything somehow...
		GenericHardmodeDialogue1: Just between us two, if you happen to possess a sword made of fish, try throwing it into some weird liquid.
		MushroomDialogue: I had a dream where you showed me all of these alchemy mushrooms in a glowing mushroom biome while shopping with me. I think you did that after defeating a weird stone construct powered by solar energy.
		SerpentAscendDialogue: I heard that in its dying moments, a serpent will ascend to become a wyrm. Maybe it's an act of mercy, an apology from their ancestors for stripping them of their primal forms. Truth or not, it is a beautiful thought to hold onto.
		ImposterDialogue: Oh hey, that's a cool name you got there, reminds me of someone. Oh? You are feeling weird? You must have eaten something bad.
		#Below is help dialogue
		ColdHellHelp: Somewhere in the western edge of the underworld caverns we detected some sort of breach. The most concerning part about it is the fact that energy itself becomes stagnant around that area. It's worth investigating, but we should be careful.
		DimensiumHelp: You can find Dimensium by doing many different things. Killing, mining, fishing, and so much more.
		KingsCapHelp: You know that mushroom forest nearby? If you wait long enough, you may find a mushroom that is larger than the others. You may wake it up using a unique fungus only found in that forest.
		TouchGrassHelp: Go outside
		#Below is quest dialogue
		FlashQuestStart: Hey, I thought you could help me out right now, I need some objects for something important. If you were to bring me 10 Frost Scales, 2 mice and around 5 Dimensium that would be great. What do I need them for? Well... I can tell you, if you bring me these things.
		FlashQuestClear: Thank you so much! With this I could create a magic construct in the image of one I miss alot. Here, you can take him with you for a while, he might be a nice little support.
		#Below is tpose dialogue
		Tpose: Help me, I'm stuck.
		#Below is arrival dialogue
		AdminArrival1: eugh
		AdminArrival2: Th... thanks, I anticipated a longer waiting time but here we are.
		AdminArrival3: It doesn't really matter how I am, rather it matters how this world is doing. My name is John God and I'm the creator of this dimension... well, this world, just to make it more understandable for you.
		AdminArrival4: Yes I know I know, meeting god is all grand and crazy, but there are more important matters to attent to.
		AdminArrival5: This world is going towards its demise, all because of sudden energy surges that were detected everywhere. I need help figuring out how to stop this or else everything is doomed.
		AdminArrival6: You seem confused.
		AdminArrival7: Yes... yes... I apologize, someone as uninvolved as you can't understand this right away. All you need to know for now is that I need someone's help and since you were the one to summon me, you must do for now.
		AdminArrival8: Well... let's just say there are complications with my "godhood". I'm sorry if that seems untrustworthy, but I cannot provide any more explanations just now.
		AdminArrival9: Very well, if you don't mind I will occupy one of your dwellings for the time being. I need some space to develop tech after all.
	}

	Taraha: {
		GenericDialogue1: Hello, welcome, trade rarities?
		GenericDialogue2: *eldritch gibberish*
		GenericDialogue3: Madness is lurking, be careful.
		GenericDialogue4: The LIGHT, so bright, so bright!
		GenericDialogue5: You ask why acorns needed? Taraha has to plant lots of acorns. Taraha wants own woods, big trees, many trees.
		GenericDialogue6: Has human ever tried finding sparkly soup? Sparkly soup somewhere behind humid place with stingy insects. Need to dig deep.
		GenericDialogue7: Taraha love this dimension, so much energy, feels comfy.
		GenericDialogue8: Taraha sees many persons here petting small fluffy creature. Taraha not know why food is being pet.
		GenericHardmodeDialogue1: Taraha traded wax for superpowerful relic the other day. Funny man thought wax was holy blood from deity.
		GenericHardmodeDialogue2: Taraha feel so many different signatures around. Why so many people here who don't belong?
		AdminDialogue: "{0} is good friend, traded much with Taraha, always give yummy crystal."
		DapperDialogue: Taraha talked to small mushroom boy about mushrooms earlier. Taraha really wanted lollipop but boy didn't want to trade for anything Taraha provided. Taraha is suffering, wants lollipop.
		BloodMoonDialogue: Taraha will bite hand off if human keeps staring.
		SlimeRainDialogue: Yum yum, gelatin heaven!
		ShadeItemDialogue: Shaded eye, Taraha can smell it. Belongs to friend, friend must be very trusty to give you gift like this. Say hello for Taraha when human meet friend.
		LollipopDialogue: Taraha can feel it. Human has lollipop. Give! Give now!
		SmileyDialogue: The king, empty, alone, withering...
		FeudalDialogue: Taraha know Umos, bad influence, he speak nonsense!
	}

	Dappercap: {
		FatherDialogue: DAD, GET THE HELL AWAY FROM HERE!
		UncleDialogue: OMG uncle, hi!
		ClothTruffleDialogue: So, sometimes I see {0} sneak into {0}'s house at night. You think there is something going on between them?
		AldinDialogue: I once met this awesome mushroom enthusiast, he was pretty chill and cool. He told me he wanted to find 7 mushrooms to do whatever, probably bend space-time or something. Anyways, he disappeared without a trace and I have not seen him since then.
		RocketDialogue: So I talked to this guy once who really seemed to like mushrooms, it was a nice conversation until he mentioned he preferred my dad over my uncle. I was like 'DUDE HOW?' and he kept going with how awesome he is. I told him to shroom himself and left him alone with a moldy one, hope the smell unrots his brain.
		GenericDialogue1: My uncle is so cool, unlike my boring as hell dad. He EVEN GLOWS, can you believe that??
		GenericDialogue2: Hey between you and me, I'm pretty sure my uncle is a hallucinogenic!!
		GenericDialogue3: I had this friend of mine named Malcolm, I got several awesome mushrooms from him, but then he suddenly stopped, saying something like "I have to be a better person". Bleh... weirdo.
		GenericDialogue4: Dem mushromz hit hart todai
		GenericDialogue6: Sometimes my dad was so annoying that I told him to finally go get some milk.
		GenericDialogue7: I heard there is a kingdom full of mushroom people, but it's not ruled by a mushroom, do you think it's real?
		GenericDialogue8: Yo, would be awesome if you were to meet my uncle. If you bring me like, 5 of these Hovercaps, I'm going to give you something that will definitely draw his attention. Why I need those caps? Well I find it really funny to use them as a frisbee.
		GenericDialogue8B: So, my uncle thought you killed my dad and stole the ring. That is very unfortunate, but tell ME. Did you two have an epic fight? Did you? Did you?
		#Below is Alch Mushroom dialogue
		TradeSuccess1: Yo awesome, take these for your work.
		TradeSuccess2: Thanks, my other contact will really appreciate these!
		TradeFail1: Idk if you understand the concept of trading but you do indeed need to give me something of interest, this isn't god damn donation central.
		TradeFail2: Hello? You understand me? You need to give thingie so I give thingie. So GET your ass out unless you need something important.
		MadnessTrade: HOLY COW! I have no idea where you found this but these mushrooms are EXTREMELY rare. There is only one species in my possession that I could give you for such a beauty.
		DyeItemTrade: Oh thanks, how did you know I was hungry?
		GlowTrade: Alright, here ya go bro. I stole this from my dad to sell it but apperantly it belongs to my uncle. Try to give it back so you two can get to know eachother!
		#Below is first time talk dialogue
		FirstTalk1: I saw you gave my dad a good thrashing, so I guess you're cool.
		FirstTalk2: Yes bro, you don't know how much I hate that guy, hope he went to cry in a corner. I'm Deadly Dappercap btw, the deadliest fungus in town, I love to get around and gather some really funky shrooms. Let's say you bring me some valuable things and I'll give you some of them. But if anyone asks, they aren't from me, understood?
		FirstTalk3: Good to know. So you bring me rare fauna and I give you some pricey fungi, that or you buy them for a Dapper deluxe price.
		#Below is box dialogue
		Box: Ey, go away, you are going to reveal my location if you keep talking to me. I will not come out until I know its safe again.
		#Below is reality shroom event dialogue
		AldinGrab1: I don't even know this mushroom, thats how rare it must be. It makes me feel weird though, so I'm not sure if I want this. WHAT THE HECK!?
		AldinGrab2: Well... that was something I guess.
	}

	Cultissima: {
		GenericDialogue1: Yes, I own a collection of glasses. Why do you ask?
		GenericDialogue2: Sometimes I question how high your horse can get before you can't get off of it anymore.
		GenericDialogue3: I know more than most people should, and the best part is, I know more things than I even know. Does that make any sense? Of course it doesn't, it has never made sense.
		AnglerDialogue: It's honestly fascinating how many different unusual uses {0} keeps finding for every fish species he comes across.
		GoggleDialogue: Wow, who sold you those glasses? I wouldn't put these in my collection even if they were worth a million bucks.
		ShadesDialogue: *finger guns*
		SteamGoggleDialogue: steamy
		#Below is first interaction dialogue
		FirstDialogue1: Hello, I was called here by Avaeris.
		FirstDialogue2: I have naturally connected to that bestiary of yours, so whatever you kill can be viewed and studied by me. I may be able to give some tips and/or insight on certain beings. And yes, I�ll do it whether you like it or not, this knowledge is too valuable.
		#Below is soul read dialogue
		SlimeSoulInsert: Ah, that big blue slime. I'm kinda curious how this one got so powerful.
		SlimeSoulRead1: Heh funny, even his soul is sticky. Wait why..?
		SlimeSoulRead2: Looks like it was once divided into many smaller slimes, until...
		SlimeSoulRead3: Ah, something about a bright flash and then... wait why is there another factor here?
		SlimeSoulReadDone: Alright, so it seems that this guy has partially fused with the soul of the person inside. Likely during the event of his creation.
		MushmonSoulInsert: Ohhh, royalty, how cooool! Seriously though, this monarch has chased many people out of his land before. I'm curious as to why.
		MushmonSoulRead1: Wow, the memory fragments in here go farther back than expected, but they are too blurry because this one spore is not enough.
		MushmonSoulRead2: Hmm. Hmmmm. There is something hidden very deep, something... ancient...
		MushmonSoulRead3: There is a bright light, and now there is will, more than before... interesting...
		MushmonSoulReadDone: The depths of this echo seem to indicate a faded light. You may be able to tap into this memory to see it for yourself.
		EyeSoulInsert: First small flying eyes now this. I shouldn't be surprised honestly, I've seen weirder things.
		EyeSoulRead1: Why do I feel watched?
		EyeSoulRead2: Hell no, I feel like the more I stare into this soul, the more intensily it stares back.
		EyeSoulRead3: Eldritch one... you shall taint no more... Avert your gaze at once! What? I think I got lost in thought just now, but it seems the eerie stare has left?
		EyeSoulReadDone: This "Eye of Cthulhu" isn't really part of Cthulhu at all, but it still seems to bear its signature. Wait, how do I even know this? Is that a correct fact?
		FungusSoulInsert: Another royal one, I see. This one leads the faithful from what I've seen.
		FungusSoulRead1: Interesting... the memory fragments are just as old as the red one's. They are still barely readable.
		FungusSoulRead2: Somehow after reading the first and now this one, I seem to understand them slightly better. Are they connected somehow?
		FungusSoulRead3: It's talking to itself? No it is talking to someone else, someone close.
		FungusSoulReadDone: A symbiotic relationship! That's it. This guy is actually two entities in one working in tandem. It seems like a beautiful relationship, but there seems to be some struggle underneath.
		EaterSoulInsert: Those corruption worms are genuinely disgusting, they make my skin crawl. Do I have to do this one? Fiiineeee-
		EaterSoulRead1: This is just as disgusting as I- Oh...
		EaterSoulRead2: This- this is awful, this is terrible.
		EaterSoulRead3: Wow, I didn't know it was this bad.
		EaterSoulReadDone: I feel kind of sorry now for being so mean. These creatures are suffering from their birth, plagued by neverending hunger. Turn this curse into your ally!
		BrainSoulInsert: A mind with a soul? That is the most absurd of things I've heard all day. What? You are serious..?
		BrainSoulRead1: Wow, this is, this is deep... It's too deep, it shouldn't be.
		BrainSoulRead2: It's like a cosmic abyss, impossibly bent.
		BrainSoulRead3: Everything about this thing makes me uncomfortable, the imprint made on this soul is malicious, desparate and hateful.
		BrainSoulReadDone: I don't say this often, but I'm glad this thing is dead, and please just take this away from me now. The power of thought it wielded is destructive. Please use it carefully...
		BeeSoulInsert: You killed a queen bee? Why? There is literally no reason for that.
		BeeSoulRead1: I see... well... I see...
		BeeSoulRead2: OH MY GOD! You were right to kill this one, she was completely overdosed on honey.
		BeeSoulRead3: No seriously there is nothing interesting here.
		BeeSoulReadDone: I'm gonna bee honest, this is the most underwhelming one you've shown me so far. At least there is some power to claim?
		SkeletonSoulInsert: Skeletron. Who named that thing, the old man? Well nevermind that, I sense some evil inside this one.
		SkeletonSoulRead1: Its makeup is simple, yet there is some complexity under the first layers.
		SkeletonSoulRead2: The imprint bears runes... and there is... hmmm... it's all curses, no will.
		SkeletonSoulRead3: I can see traces of stronger magic clinging to it, yet I can't find out where and from where.
		SkeletonSoulReadDone: Well, this thing was literally just a huge clump of curses that stuck together like glue. It had barely enough "will" to keep going on its own.
		SmileySoulInsert: Oh, the smiling dark one gave you that? Well, let's see what it hides within.
		SmileySoulRead1: This one is crystal clear, as if the fragment itself wants to be deciphered. Really strange but welcome.
		SmileySoulRead2: It tells the story of a sole will awakening amidst darkness. It challenges its origins as more wills awaken.
		SmileySoulRead3: Those many wills defend the first, giving their lives. The first escapes with others of its kind, gaining the power to live for themselves.
		SmileySoulReadDone: This is inspirational, a single individual fighting for freedom with a will shaped just for this purpose.
		DeerSoulInsert: Oh the snow monster, you took it down. I've heard its gurgly roars in the night a lot.
		DeerSoulRead1: I see a dark place...
		DeerSoulRead2: There are people around a campfire. The point of view is drawing closer.
		DeerSoulRead3: Oh... oh no, this is brutal. I think I'm gonna spare you the details.
		DeerSoulReadDone: Well it's a monster, so it kills and destroys. I just didn't like how satisfied it looked after being finished.
		WallSoulInsert: You got this from a what? A wall of literal flesh? Actually upon closer inspection of your bestia- what the hell!
		WallSoulRead1: This soul is- it's overflowing with life. There is hundreds of individuals trapped inside..! I don't like this.
		WallSoulRead2: There is no harmony here either, they seem to be fighting even while being nothing but spiritual energy.
		WallSoulRead3: You can hear screams of anger, war cries. What the hell is going on?
		WallSoulReadDone: Something like this shouldn't exist, such a conentrated cluster of soul energy. Whatever the case, I have heard whispers, maybe if you listen close enough...
		QueenSlimeSoulInsert: Another slime's soul? If I had a silver coin for every time you brought me one, I would have two silver coins.
		QueenSlimeSoulRead1: This one seems similar to the king, starting out as a small group of individuals.
		QueenSlimeSoulRead2: That crystal inside her seems to have been formed during the incident that unleashed all the spiritual energy. That's still your fault by the way.
		QueenSlimeSoulRead3: It's not just a crystal, there is something inside. Another trace of soul energy bound to the crystal.
		QueenSlimeSoulReadDone: It seems that yet again, someone's soul was fused with the slimes that make up this big one. Makes you wonder who that someone was before this.
		TwinSoulInsert: More flying eyes? I won't even question it anymore. Just make sure this one isn't as creepy.
		TwinSoulRead1: I see... a city? Steel wherever you look and a darkened sky.
		TwinSoulRead2: They were given purpose here, "fly far, see far". The banging of metal against metal can be heard.
		TwinSoulRead3: After enough tests, they were sent away, far away, to look for something, or... someone. Once they arrived here they took on the shape of what they saw first.
		TwinSoulReadDone: These two were machines built to scout and eventually find a very specific person. The thing that terrifies me though, is that Avaeris's face appears as the target.
		DestroyerSoulInsert: Of course there is a massive metallic worm that shoots lasers, why not. Actually upon further consideration, who could build something like that in this primitive world?
		DestroyerSoulRead1: There is a city of steel, friction is in the air.
		DestroyerSoulRead2: It was given a purpose here, "Dig. Dig deep". The metal screeches as frames are put into place.
		DestroyerSoulRead3: After realizing the ground beneath is not suitable for excavation, it was sent far away to accompany three others and gather fuel for them. Once it arrived here, it took on the shape of what it was first.
		DestroyerSoulReadDone: This machine was once an excavator that was sent on a mission with its purpose being a fuel gatherer.
		PrimeSoulInsert: So you are telling me there is somehow a mechanical version of the dungeon's curse. This doesn't make any god damn sense.
		PrimeSoulRead1: A huge city as far as one can see.
		PrimeSoulRead2: A purpose was granted here, "Eviscerate. Defend". Metal echoes through the empty streets.
		PrimeSoulRead3: When curiosity was satisfied, it was sent away from home. It travelled alongside its companions whom it was tasked to defend. Once it arrived here, it took on the shape of what it was first.
		PrimeSoulReadDone: It was a weapon of destruction born from a simple curious mind, then repurposed to defend other machines it travelled with. Well, it seems to have failed miserably.
		PlanteraSoulInsert: So. A plant? How does a plant have- You know what, let's just look inside and answer that question before asking it.
		PlanteraSoulRead1: I see a regular pink bulb waiting to bloom. Robed figures approach it, their gazes can be felt even with their faces hidden.
		PlanteraSoulRead2: The bulb breathes, it lives, it feels. The robed figures laugh and celebrate, not noticing the small flowers they stepped on. I think I know what happens next.
		PlanteraSoulRead3: The newly birthed jungle gurdian lashes out and consumes every single one of its creators... wow.
		PlanteraSoulReadDone: Plantera was once an ordinary flower that was gives a will to live, but no mind to think, so she took the task she was given to heart. She killed all her creators after they accidentily hurt the jungle.
		GolemSoulInsert: This one will be interesting, an automaton built from nothing but brick and energy? Hell yeah.
		GolemSoulRead1: There is a lot of desperation within this one. I see fear and paranoia caused by disasters happening all around.
		GolemSoulRead2: Many hands build a figure brick by brick, probably hoping that it will protect them.
		GolemSoulRead3: They form a core from solar energy and insert it into the construct, that's impressive.
		GolemSoulReadDone: This golem was built as a protector deity, modeled after a real mythological being from lihzahrd culture.
		DukeSoulInsert: The fishron, fierce predators of the seas. A while ago I picked up a book when visiting a village and I loved their stories about these guys.
		DukeSoulRead1: Dark waters, nothing but the void all around. The fishron stalks its prey aaaand... BOOM! He got the little worm!
		DukeSoulRead2: Wait there is more to this. A storm is brewing, but the fishron won't seek shelter, it instead flies straight into it.
		DukeSoulRead3: What's this? A hand reaches out to pet the fishron and, there is a large siluette within a thunderstorm.
		DukeSoulReadDone: Yeah I knew these guys love worms, but the part with that mysterious siluette was certainly weird.
		EmpressSoulInsert: The Empress of Light... Yes I need to see what her emotions have to say.
		EmpressSoulRead1: I see ancient chains, ancient energies. An eternity of servitude? What? A war, another war, then peace. A door closes and it becomes dark.
		EmpressSoulRead2: After a long time of loneliness, the door opens again, and what she finds is yet another war...
		EmpressSoulRead3: But then everyone disappeared so she could roam free. Of her own volition, she found another to protect.
		EmpressSoulReadDone: Bound by an eternal contract to serve and defend as a guardian, only to be discarded when she's no longer needed. What an awful fate.
		CultistSoulInsert: Cultists... sometimes I wonder what moves people to found such groups. Well, may we find out?
		CultistSoulRead1: I see regret... yet it is born of ego. A man finds the shrine of a forgotten deity.
		CultistSoulRead2: He believed it must be god, so he devotes his entire life to resurrect it and on the way he came across a light.
		CultistSoulRead3: The light encouraged him to continue his journey, I don't know why though.
		CultistSoulReadDone: The person behind the mask was once a devoted man of faith, but his longing to serve ruined him. There is still something left that refuses to let go.
		MoonSoulInsert: The lord of the moon you say, well whatever it actually was, it was TERRIFYING!
		MoonSoulRead1: I see... uhm... how do I say this? I can't see anything. It's like it's empty.
		MoonSoulRead2: WAIT, there is something very, VERY deep inside. So deep I almost missed it. Cthulhu, eldritch entity.
		MoonSoulRead3: It's a husk, grown to house a missing soul. The one I'm analyzing right now is nothing but an empty artificial imitation.
		MoonSoulReadDone: So the Moon Lord was nothing but a vessel for a lost soul. Its mind was empty, so was this soul. Glad it was destroyed.
		TorchSoulInsert:
			'''
			Torch God? TORCH GOD?! What the f-
			A-ahem, sorry it seems like I just had a stroke there.
			'''
		TorchSoulRead1: Mhm mhm, yes I see fire, fire and who guessed it... MORE FIRE!
		TorchSoulRead2: Wow, there is so much god damn fire in there.
		TorchSoulRead3: My eyes are burning it's so bright.
		TorchSoulReadDone: As previously observed, this deity is specificly tuned to keep torches aflame. You can now use its power to generate infinite torches.
	}

	VanillaNPCDialogue: {
		Truffle: {
			Dapper1: My brother Malcom, always talked about little Dappercap when he visited. But then he eventually stopped showing up, and not even dapper knows where he is now. He just said Malcom was gonna make amends for his crimes.
			Dapper2: Despite his looks and behavior, Dappercap is the scarlet prince. But even with this title and the respect he gains from it, he ran away and never returned home. Even Umos is in mild distraught by this.
			Umos1: Our glowing royalty, Umos, he is what keeps us going, that light in the dark. While I don't 100% agree with his ways, he is still our light.
			Umos2: It is really scary to be granted sentience out of nowhere. I felt lost at first, but then I was guided by a light, it was his light. These are times of peace for my kin, something not many have.
			Umos3: Many creatures in the dark caverns come to our glowing sanctuaries. Those often bear hostility however, which makes them intruders rather than guests. Somehow Umos sees them as worthy, saying that all deserve salvation.
			UmosDead: I know you defeated our apostle in battle. I have no grudge against you, it must have been a misunderstanding. He can be very defensive against outsiders.
			Unimush1: I feel like something is pulling at my mind recently, it makes me very uneasy...
			Unimush2: Since recently I hear my brother call to me from afar sometimes, but when I look, there is nobody there.
			Unimush3: My nightmares have gotten worse, I feel like everyone wants to consume me.
		}

		Wizard.Carces: I once heard of a settlement called Carces. Apperantly it was a humble town that was famous for its so called 'Twin Libraries', which would contain ancient manuscripts. I would love to get my hands on some of those, but sadly the town was burned down many years ago.
	}
}

AdminTpose.DisplayName: Admin Tpose

Admin: {
	TownNPCMood: {
		Princess_LovesNPC: "{NPCName} is such a fascinating person, he always shows me those amazing magic devices he has. One was even able to conjur up plates of some of the most divine cookies on it."
		LikeNPC_Princess: The small pink lady, yes {NPCName}. I feel weirdly at ease when I'm around her, so at ease in fact that I accidentily keep telling her things that nobody's supposed to know.
		HateNPC: I can't stand being near {NPCName}, he reminds me of long forgotten sins.
		DislikeNPC: "{NPCName} always wants to discuss spells with me and keeps calling me a fellow wizard. I'm not a magician, I'm a scientist!"
		LoveNPC: I'm glad that {NPCName} was able to come here too, she is a very valuable member for our cause. I would also not forgive myself if something bad happened since she is personal protection.
		LikeNPC: I like {NPCName}. She is a great help for some of my experiments, even if she doesn't understand half of it.
		HateBiome: I should go somewhere else, whenever I have a thought it gets disrupted by these god damn pixies, they are SO noisy.
		DislikeBiome: This tundra is such an awful place for my machinery. The energy flow just keeps slowing due to the cold.
		LikeBiome: Being underground is doing a good job for me. Not many interferences happening to disturb any experiment.
		LoveBiome: Ahh, the forest, it's so perfect. Beautiful, quiet and perfectly tempered.
		HateCrowded: I hate how many people are around. It's too reminiscent of the old times.
		DislikeCrowded: It's starting to get a little full around here
		LoveSpace: It's really nice having time to think alone sometimes, the large amount of space really contributes.
		FarFromHome: Not having the ability to teleport by myself is so tedious. My place is SO far away.
		NoHome: Now that you summoned me, I'm in desperate need of a place to stay, you got anything?
		Content: I feel alright.
	}

	MiscText: {
		AdminResponse1: ...
		AdminResponse2: Are you alright?
		AdminResponse3: Wait really?? That's insane!
		AdminResponse4: But wait
		AdminResponse5: I-
		AdminResponse6: It's just a lot of information all at once.
		AdminResponse7: But if you are god, why don't do it yourself?
		AdminResponse8: Well then... if you insist, I will believe this for now.
		AdminResponse9: Okay?
	}

	DisplayName: Administrator
}

